<title>USA: Handleman Q3 net boosted by intl sales.</title>
<headline>Handleman Q3 net boosted by intl sales.</headline>
<dateline>TROY, Mich. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Handleman Co said Thursday that higher international sales and higher gross margins helped earnings climb in its fiscal third quarter ended January 31, even as overall sales declined.</p>
<p>Handleman, which distributes music, video, books and software, said adding new customers in Mexico, Brazil and Argentina helped international sales climb to $41.9 million in the quarter from $26.1 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Handleman shares were up 5/8 at 9-1/4.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
